<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton rates mixed amid low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton rates mixed amid low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates remained mixed on Saturday amid low demand and dealers said prices were likely to ease as mill owners were short of funds.</p>
<p>&quot;Prices are under pressure because mill owners are short of funds and exporters are on the sidelines,&quot; dealer Kuhshi Ram said.</p>
<p>In the kerb, NIAB-78 variety was quoted at around 1,900 ($47.24) per maund (37.32 kg).  </p>
<p>Saturday's official spot rates issued by the Karachi Cotton Association in rupees per maund including 10 percent sales tax:</p>
<p>					   Saturday	   Previous</p>
<p>    NIAB-78 (1996/97 crop)	 2,322.50	   2,344.50</p>
<p>    K-68    (1996/97 crop)	 2,537.00	   2,537.00</p>
<p>    MNH-93  (1996/97 crop)	 2,547.00	   2,547.00</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
